    "updated_at": "2016-05-23T11:06:23Z",
    "body": "> (We still have issues if a script does for example `dataTransfer.setData('text/uri-list', 'http://foo:bar')` - but I think in that case we should just return the input as-is without any attempts to parse it..?)\n\nCertainly the spec for `setData` just passes through. For `getData` it says\n\n> If convert-to-URL is true, then parse result as appropriate for text/uri-list data, and then set result to the first URL from the list, if any, or the empty string otherwise. [RFC2483]\n\nI don't know if it means to try to parse each URL or not. It seems there are no processing requirements for that format; the RFC says\n\n>    The text/uri-list MIME Media Type is specified in Section 5. This\n>    Media Type is merely a suggestion for experimental systems that need\n>    a simple implementation. It is included here merely as an example to\n>    show completeness (however simple it may be).\n\n☹️\n",
