    "created_at": "2016-05-23T11:07:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-23T11:07:27Z",
    "body": "Ah, OK. We have similar issues when HTML is placed on the clipboard - we'd like URLs in the source to be resolved (since the paste target can't be expected to resolve any relative URLs correctly) and while I'm saying something about this in the clipboard spec I'm not handling parsing failures. Also, those details should be in the DataTransfer spec.\n\nSo, first thought: I don't really expect the DataTransfer API to make any specific guarantee about the correctness/validity of URLs. If the URL of a dragged A element doesn't parse, well - just do element.getAttribute('href') and use whatever junk is there..\n\nSecond thought: what about security? If we don't do anything to validate the input, scripts can push any sort of binary junk to the clipboard, labelled as URL lists, and try to exploit paste targets that expect URLs to be URLs and have exploitable faults in their parsers..!?\n",
